course: dictionary
lesson: 3912
title: Frisian: a place, a language, a cow
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Some words name a place, a people, a language or an animal. «Frisian» is one of these words. It can describe something, as in «Frisian Islands», or name something, as in «a Frisian». Context tells you which job it does.
explain: Look at the clues in «English is a Germanic language, a cousin of German, Dutch and Frisian.» Frisian sits in a list of languages, next to German and Dutch, so it must be a language. The sentence also says it is a cousin of English.
explain: Frisian always starts with a capital letter, because it names a place, a people, or a language. You may also see Friesian, another spelling. In a farm story, a Friesian is a cow, so the context shows you it is not a language.
fact: Frisian means from or belonging to Friesland or the Frisian Islands, on the North Sea coast in the Netherlands and Germany.
fact: Frisian is the language spoken there, and it is the closest living language to English.
fact: «Bread, butter and green cheese is good English and good Frisian» is a saying that shows how close the two languages are.
fact: A Frisian, or Friesian, is also a breed of black-and-white dairy cow that gives lots of milk.
exercise: «English is a Germanic language, a cousin of German, Dutch and Frisian.» In this sentence, what is Frisian? | A colour | A type of bread | A kind of weather | *A language
exercise: Ella reads «a Friesian cow in the field». What kind of animal is a Friesian? | A bird that sings at dawn | A fish from the North Sea | A large black horse with a long tail | *A black-and-white dairy cow
exercise: Which language is the closest living language to English? | Japanese | Swahili | Welsh | *Frisian
test: The Frisian Islands lie along the North Sea coast of which two countries? | Norway and Sweden | Italy and Greece | France and Spain | *The Netherlands and Germany
test: In «a Frisian», what kind of word is Frisian? | *A noun, because it names a person or thing | A verb, because it is an action | An adverb, because it tells how | A preposition, because it shows place
exam: The saying «Bread, butter and green cheese is good English and good Frisian» shows that | English and Frisian have no link at all | *English and Frisian are very close relatives | English comes only from Frisian | Frisian is a kind of cheese
